  "raw_text": "211\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Blasi Sturka 22:3\n):\n \nEbraham titan pali buan, mahka ai birikuka ba satil mangkan\n \n–\n \nAbraham got up early in the\nmorning and immediately saddled his donkey\n \n/ Abrahán se levantó temprano en la mañana e inmediatamente ensilló su\nburro)\n\nSauhkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nSaukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto destroy, to ruin, to spoil, to demolish, to wreck, to harm\n \n/ destruir, arruinar, estropear,\ndemoler, dañar, deshacer, aniquilar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb53\n):\n \nJoiad\ná\n \nadar yan Baal tempelka ba slingbaia bara aidul nani ba sauhkaia.\n \n–\n \nJehoiada gave the order to tear down the\n\ntemple of Baal and destroy the idols.\n \n/ Joiad\ná\n \ndio la orden de derribar el templo de Baal y destruir a los ídolos.\n)\n\nDanh sauhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto destroy and make gone, to completely destroy\n \n/ destruir y\n \nhacer\n \ndesaparecer, destruir\n\ncompletamente\n\nDiara saura pali bara sauhki tatikra ba\n \n(\nwqu\n-\n05/20\n-\nDan\niel\n \n11:31\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nThe disgusting thing that causes\n\ndesolation\n \n/ L\na cosa\n \nrepugnante que causa desolación\n\nKupia sauhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto offend, to dishearten, to annoy, to anger\n \n/ ofender, desanimar, molestar, enojar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf23\n):\n \nisti pali kupiam sauhkpara\n \n–\n \ndo not quickly get upset\n \n/ no te enfades rápidamente)\n\nKupia sauhkan\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado,\nadj)\n \n–\n \noffended, disheartened, angered, angry\n \n/\n \nofendió,\n \no\nfendido\n,\n\ndesanimó\n,\n \ndesanimado,\n \nenojó,\n \nenojado\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb56\n):\n \nJehova yawan nani wal ai kupia sauhkan sa\n \n–\n \nJehovah is angry with us\n \n/ Jehová está enojado con\n\nnosotros\n)\n\nKupia\n \nsauhki bîla\n \n–\n \noffensive word, disheartening word, word that causes annoyance, word that angers\n \n/\n\npalabra ofensiva, palabra\n \ndesalentadora, palabra que causa molestia, palabra que enoja\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n12\n):\n \nkupia sauhki b\nîla\n \nnani yus munpara\n \n–\n \ndo not use offensive/disheartening words/expressions\n \n/ no use\n\npalabras/expresiones ofensivas/desalentadoras\n)\n\nMarit lâka sauhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto commit adultery, to ruin marriage, to destroy marriage\n \n/ cometer adulterio, arruinar\n\nel matrimonio, destruir el matrimonio\n\nMarit lâka sasauhkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nadulterer, marriage wrecker\n \n/ adúltero, destructor de\n\nmatrimonio\n\nNina sauhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ruin a name, to slander, to do harm to a name\n \n/ arruinar un nombre, calumniar, dañar a\n\nun nombre\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n08/19\n):\n \nJisas ba kasakka lâka latwan kaikisa bara dîa ai aisika nina sauhkaia sip ba misbara kaikisa\n \n–\n \nJesus\n\nloves righteousness and hates what (anything that) could hurt his father’s name\n \n/ Jesús ama la justicia y odia lo que\n\n(cualquier cosa\n \nque\n) pueda dañar el nombre de su padre\n)\n\nNina sasauhkra\n \n(\nlv,dict\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nslanderer, devil\n \n/ calumniador, diablo\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nslanderer\n \n/ calumniador\n \n–\n \nNina aisasara\n-\ndb\n,\n \nDahra kwakwahkra\n-\ndb\n,\n \nNina sasauhkra\n-\ndict,lv\n)\n\nRau sauhkaia\n \n(\na/t:\n \nRausauhkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto mistreat, to abuse, to persecute, to destroy or damage\n \nproperty\n \n/\n\nmaltratar, abusar, perseguir, destruir o dañar bienes\n\nSasauhkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ndestroyer, spoiler, wrecker\n \n/ destructor,\n \nda\nñador, dañino, arruinador\n\nLâka sasauhkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nbreaker of the law\n \n/ violador de la ley\n\nSauhkan\n \nyuika nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nruins, rubble\n \n/ ruinas, escombros\n\nSauhkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndestruction, ruin, disaster\n \n/ destrucción, ruina, desastre\n\nPrari sauhkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhurricane\n \n/ huracán\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/19\n):\n \nPrari nani sauhkanka mita pât brin nani ba\n \n–\n \nVictims of the\n \nhurricanes\n \n/ Víctimas de los\n\nhuracanes\n)\n\nSauh\nkanka\n \nHilp Yabaia Daknika\n \n–\n \nDisaster Relief Department\n \n/\n \nDepartamento de Labores de Socorro\n\nSauh\nkanka\n \nnani Hilp\n \nMunai\na Daknika\n \n–\n \nDisaster Relief\n \nCommittee\n \n/\n \nComité de Socorro\n\nSauh\nkanka\n \nnani\n \nh\nilp\n \nm\nunaia\n \nwarkka\n \n–\n \nd\nisaster\n \nr\nelief\n \n(work)\n \n/\n \nlabores de s\nocorro\n\nTasba sauhkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnatural disaster\n \n/ desastre natural\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/20\n):\n \nYawan sut d\nî\na sip ba kat daukaia sa, tasba sauhkanka kum kau balras kainara ridi kaia\n\ndukiara.\n \n–\n \nWe must do all that we\n \nare able to do in order to be ready before a natural disaster comes.\n \n/ Debemos\n\nhacer todo lo que podamos para estar preparados antes de que ocurra un desastre natural.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n11/20\n):\n \nD\nî\na muni d\nî\na wan wi ba aman wali alki daukaia sa tasba sauhkanka mapara ridi kaia\n\ndukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhy must we listen carefully to apply what is being said to us with regards to natural disasters in\n\norder to be ready?\n \n/\n \n¿Por qué debemos escuchar atentamente para aplicar lo que se nos dice sobre los desastres\n\nnaturales para estar preparados?\n)\n\nSauhki\n \ntikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto destroy\n \ncompletely\n, to\n \ncompletely\n \nruin, to spoil\n \ncompletely\n, to demolish completely\n \n/\n\ndestruir por completo, arruinar por completo, estropear por completo, demoler por completo",
